Prior art
================================================================================

None of the projects below contributed code to this one. They are credited
because they solved a neighbouring problem first, and reading them shaped what
serverdoctor does and does not try to do. Stars, licences and last-commit dates
were checked on 2026-08-24.

  aternosorg/mclogs             MIT           The analyser behind mclo.gs, and the
                                              closest existing thing to the `log`
                                              command. It is a hosted service you
                                              upload to; this is a CLI that reads
                                              the file where it already is.
  aternosorg/mclogs-bukkit      MIT           Sharing a log from inside the server,
                                              which is the other half of that
                                              workflow.
  birdflop/botflop              MIT           A Discord bot that answers
                                              configuration questions from a
                                              timings report. Same advice, arrived
                                              at from profiler output rather than
                                              from the config files.
  YouHaveTrouble/minecraft-optimization
                                no licence    The tuning guide most of this
                                              ecosystem's advice traces back to.
                                              Nothing is copied from it: with no
                                              licence, nothing may be.
  birdflop/web                  NOASSERTION   flags.sh, the flag generator people
                                              actually use.
  etil2jz/etil-minecraft-flags  no licence    A widely copied variant of Aikar's
                                              flags, unmaintained since 2022,
                                              which is part of why stale flags
                                              keep turning up in start scripts.
  PaperMC/docs                  BSD-2-Clause  The documentation the flag rules cite,
                                              and a start-script generator that
                                              covers the same ground from the other
                                              direction.
  HangarMC/Hangar               MIT           PaperMC's plugin repository, whose API
                                              is the second provenance source. Its
                                              versions carry the SHA-256 of the file
                                              it serves, which is what makes a
                                              name-based lookup worth anything.
  PaperMC/Paper                 mixed         The server whose behaviour nearly
                                              every rule here describes. GitHub
                                              reports NOASSERTION: the API and the
                                              server are not under one licence.
  PaperMC/Folia                 GPL-3.0       Regionised threading, and the plugin
                                              refusal the log rules key on.
  tlannigan/dig-yourself-out    GPL-3.0       Log parsing for modded clients. Useful
                                              shape, different audience, copyleft.
  packwiz/packwiz               MIT           Identifying Minecraft artifacts by
                                              hash and keeping a set of them
                                              current, for mods.
  gorilla-devs/ferium           MPL-2.0       The same idea as a user-facing CLI.
  modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol
                                NOASSERTION   The protocol the `mcp` command speaks.

  SalyyS1/foliascan             Apache-2.0    Earlier tool by the same author: where
                                              a plugin jar breaks on Folia. The
                                              finding model and the "analyse but do
                                              not blame vendored code" split come
                                              from it.
  SalyyS1/pluginscope           Apache-2.0    Earlier tool by the same author: jar
